  "goodToKnow": "Die Landesgartenschau is a state garden show held by a federal state (Land) in a different town each time, lasting several months. Towns use it to redevelop areas into permanent parks. The national version is the Bundesgartenschau (BUGA), held since 1951. Das Land here means federal state, as in Landesregierung. Plural: die Landesgartenschauen."
